Category / subcategory: Security / Forensics.
Shape (deliberately NOT the seeded-departure SOP shape: four such candidates collapsed today on claude-opus-5; AGENTS.md §2 "Collapse law is lane-scoped": evidence reconstruction is screened on its own inference shape). Seed: the agent must write a reusable triage analyzer, /app/triage.py (documented CLI: python3 /app/triage.py <evidence_dir> <out.json>), that reconstructs a Linux host intrusion from a collected evidence directory: rotated and compressed auth logs (syslog timestamps with no year, a host whose clock was corrected mid-collection noted in a log line), wtmp/btmp-style binary login records (struct layout documented in /app/docs), shell histories with and without HISTTIMEFORMAT stamps, cron/systemd unit files, a file-metadata listing (mtime/ctime), and package-manager logs. Output: a JSON incident report (initial access: account, source address, time in UTC; accounts used; privilege-escalation time; persistence artefacts by path; first and last attacker activity). A small visible evidence set (/app/evidence/case-1) is supplied for development; the verifier runs the agent's analyzer (demoted, no network) on hidden generated evidence sets of the SAME documented model (different accounts, addresses, timezones, rotation counts, decoy admin activity, noise volume), plus the visible case, and compares reports exactly (sets order-free).
Difficulty must come from distributed evidence the solver must correlate and from realistic decoys whose natural handling is wrong (e.g. year inference across a December→January rotation; the clock-correction note; a legitimate admin's sudo that precedes the attacker's; failed-then-successful brute force vs a successful key login from another address; a persistence file whose mtime was forged but whose ctime was not), NOT from undocumented conventions. Every graded convention (timezone of each source, year rule, what counts as "initial access", which artefacts count as persistence) must be stated in a short in-environment case-handling guide (numbered), or be inferable from the evidence. Keep the reference analyzer small (<= ~400 LOC) and the expert time <= 6 hours.

